"authoredDate":"2025-08-27T09:58:04Z","committedDate":"2025-08-27T09:58:04Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:12:16.482Z","repositoryId":687864678,"sha":"d84e748d1ed11d3f7524d22a45c9e3b9961f923e"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","providerType":"Bot"},"email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"authoredDate":"2025-08-27T09:38:45Z","committedDate":"2025-08-27T09:38:45Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:12:16.482Z","repositoryId":687864678,"sha":"f9af8f77f3b6f8e4cade8d32bfcdac5c40688470"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","providerType":"Bot"},"email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"authoredDate":"2025-08-27T08:47:06Z","committedDate":"2025-08-27T08:47:06Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:12:16.482Z","repositoryId":687864678,"sha":"efff41d97fd0e5af3432799f3a527803ef08d7c1"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","providerType":"Bot"},"email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"authoredDate":"2025-08-27T08:31:38Z","committedDate":"2025-08-27T08:31:38Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:12:16.482Z","repositoryId":687864678,"sha":"bb82796e3ba79cea499d2ba11a447c04001f410a"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"ferdinandsalis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis-Samaden"},"authoredDate":"2025-08-27T07:37:43Z","committedDate":"2025-08-27T07:37:43Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"ferdinandsalis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis-Samaden"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:12:16.482Z","repositoryId":687864678,"sha":"1097c4d82519b9e1d211d454a70cbf5d39fabb5c"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"ferdinandsalis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis-Samaden"},"authoredDate":"2025-08-26T21:27:35Z","committedDate":"2025-08-26T21:27:35Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"ferdinandsalis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis-Samaden"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:12:16.482Z","repositoryId":687864678,"sha":"fe814027ad63565fdc7335e7eb75ac7f2f96d471"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"ferdinandsalis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis-Samaden"},"authoredDate":"2025-08-26T19:55:08Z","committedDate":"2025-08-26T19:55:08Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"ferdinandsalis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis-Samaden"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:12:16.482Z","repositoryId":687864678,"sha":"650940b202afb54b06c22988a3d4f8ee0822b784"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"ferdinandsalis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis-Samaden"},"authoredDate":"2025-08-26T19:50:01Z","committedDate":"2025-08-26T19:50:01Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"ferdinandsalis","providerType":"User"},"email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis-Samaden"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:12:16.482Z","repositoryId":687864678,"sha":"54fb7470de0a4f73302b4208e256fa754ccf4b50"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T18:12:16.482Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340520?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis","id":340520,"login":"ferdinandsalis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDUyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/60e5981d55de62adda815a36b8037fbc9b70a188/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T14:54:04Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T14:54:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix newsletter sign-up: proxy origin check and Buttondown field rename (#143)\n\n* Trust Fly''s proxy so form actions pass React Router''s origin check\n\nReact Router 7.18 compares the browser''s Origin header against the full\nrequest URL, scheme included. Behind Fly the app sees plain HTTP, so the\nrequest URL was http://www.walz.at while browsers send\nOrigin: https://www.walz.at, and every action (newsletter, Aufnahmeformular)\nwas rejected with 400 since the 7.18 upgrade.\n\nTrusting the proxy makes req.protocol honor X-Forwarded-Proto. Rate limits\nnow key on Fly-Client-Ip, which clients cannot spoof, instead of req.ip.\n\nFixes WALZ-8G\n\n* Send Buttondown the email_address field it now requires\n\nButtondown renamed the subscriber field email to email_address and rejects\nthe old name with 422 field_renamed, so newsletter sign-ups were dropped.\nAlso move to the api.buttondown.com host its docs now use.\n\n* Tell newsletter readers when Buttondown rejects their sign-up\n\nThe action ignored Buttondown''s response, so every failed sign-up still\nshowed \"Aktion Erfolgreich\". It now reports the failure to Sentry with a\nconstant message (no address) and the form shows an error instead.\nSigning up again with a known address merges into the existing subscriber\nrather than failing with Buttondown''s 400 collision. The action no longer\nechoes the address back to the client.","tree":{"sha":"5a7bc148ddd24ab63cf6bcd2b79f22bc07faa3a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/5a7bc148ddd24ab63cf6bcd2b79f22bc07faa3a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/60e5981d55de62adda815a36b8037fbc9b70a188","verification":{"payload":"tree 5a7bc148ddd24ab63cf6bcd2b79f22bc07faa3a7\nparent 8d8a29e457c1b796e39ec9f70248b4f891b1c818\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1791471244 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791471244 +0200\n\nFix newsletter sign-up: proxy origin check and Buttondown field rename (#143)\n\n* Trust Fly''s proxy so form actions pass React Router''s origin check\n\nReact Router 7.18 compares the browser''s Origin header against the full\nrequest URL, scheme included. Behind Fly the app sees plain HTTP, so the\nrequest URL was http://www.walz.at while browsers send\nOrigin: https://www.walz.at, and every action (newsletter, Aufnahmeformular)\nwas rejected with 400 since the 7.18 upgrade.\n\nTrusting the proxy makes req.protocol honor X-Forwarded-Proto. Rate limits\nnow key on Fly-Client-Ip, which clients cannot spoof, instead of req.ip.\n\nFixes WALZ-8G\n\n* Send Buttondown the email_address field it now requires\n\nButtondown renamed the subscriber field email to email_address and rejects\nthe old name with 422 field_renamed, so newsletter sign-ups were dropped.\nAlso move to the api.buttondown.com host its docs now use.\n\n* Tell newsletter readers when Buttondown rejects their sign-up\n\nThe action ignored Buttondown''s response, so every failed sign-up still\nshowed \"Aktion Erfolgreich\". It now reports the failure to Sentry with a\nconstant message (no address) and the form shows an error instead.\nSigning up again with a known address merges into the existing subscriber\nrather than failing with Buttondown''s 400 collision. The action no longer\nechoes the address back to the client.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx66MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQQEQAH49QmCmF3CCXLOYKPYG9vF3\neaz95RjDhie3LfmxKveqVLlqsw/Q5pzwjnxo/FEbCYcY0c3NjYq+RJVnp5zpcfic\nT5gM7MJO9t2SBQwkEYPdMki5EHJMx5JQ3pXtZmpfvbpRufAr4u7qY/yypgQjeeOE\nkqsuxSDxyxu/tEi2ywFawOhqq+l6FnNApMOdZPNUzP7NwydFO4SMPFFUYnsCO00o\nBKVnbF7FBiAgrDTlAi2kl3PD5bEl/FPbwXRShBRun5qwe74AKwVZo1NUhLyFosEN\nP2IN+V5UfpqQsVgvtaWPc3kgXE+CsOrOyC3Ym5/vrIq7UTI/Ds9px8xZbz0z6y5g\nVBgNG1EQ/GQLLFmZv/DDAdP7+bhJj8gyxbQfdbTmDLmMJIoKe3X9+U8Lbp7rteNP\n4X3WJ81NAlpBmk7WiMmu0yPh53lRIIRLoH5JxR+ZRzKRqPpikpVmRuqoGt8T6Xen\nPtqjblrL8Z0KNIohpEEh8GsbFF4i85N6ciNJrCHZDxFBIlhVg2U1nmv+Ds9hW+eN\n1X1gGnCRTs14XuHdbu5zVL+a/76ekzu5zatDqVsfI809STsPTWj7yVY+DPpZpd0s\nc9xg/bsS0t6K2PT+yS7aJTRYXASPru2IgZCIszVZWYMMdPsaXo85qu3Jq0EjHtZH\nkCX5fdmrMTLwQAze4hVX\n=QtG6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T14:54:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/60e5981d55de62adda815a36b8037fbc9b70a188","node_id":"C_kwDOKP_7ZtoAKDYwZTU5ODFkNTVkZTYyYWRkYTgxNWEzNmI4MDM3ZmJjOWI3MGExODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/8d8a29e457c1b796e39ec9f70248b4f891b1c818","sha":"8d8a29e457c1b796e39ec9f70248b4f891b1c818","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/8d8a29e457c1b796e39ec9f70248b4f891b1c818"}],"sha":"60e5981d55de62adda815a36b8037fbc9b70a188","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/60e5981d55de62adda815a36b8037fbc9b70a188"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340520?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis","id":340520,"login":"ferdinandsalis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDUyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/8d8a29e457c1b796e39ec9f70248b4f891b1c818/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:25:34Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:25:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Redesign the Aufnahme form on a Lernpfad design vocabulary (#142)\n\n* Design the Aufnahmeformular redesign\n\nResearch-backed spec for a parent-first, single-page form with structured\naddresses, per-field errors and a confirmation page that explains the next\nsteps. Revised after an independent design and accessibility review.\n\n* Keep exactly one title on the Aufnahme form page\n\n* Plan the Aufnahmeformular redesign implementation\n\n* Validate the Aufnahme form in one shared module\n\n* Add accessible form field primitives and 16px inputs\n\nField and FieldGroup wire hint and error ids into aria-describedby and\naria-invalid. Input and Textarea use 16px text so iOS does not zoom on\nfocus, and draw a 2px border when aria-invalid.\n\nDarken --input and --ring so form controls meet the 3:1 non-text\ncontrast of WCAG 1.4.11 (no dark-mode block exists to update):\n\n  --input  28 5% 90%       -> 28 5% 52%\n    vs --card        1.25 -> 3.68\n    vs --background  1.17 -> 3.44\n  --ring   215 20.2% 65.1% -> 215 20.2% 55%\n    vs --card        2.56 -> 3.60\n    vs --background  2.39 -> 3.36\n\nDeclare WarningCircle in the hand-maintained phosphor type shim.\n\n* Write structured addresses and school history into the Aufnahme email\n\n* Return field errors and send the office copy first from the Aufnahme action\n\n* Rebuild the Aufnahme form parent-first with structured addresses\n\n* Skip the hidden guardian address and describe each date input on the Aufnahme form\n\n* Show per-field errors with a focused summary on the Aufnahme form\n\n* Reword the stale comment in the Aufnahme loading-state test\n\n* Clear emptied optional errors and cover the submit guard reset on the Aufnahme form\n\n* Leave the newsletter box off the Aufnahme form\n\n* Show the next steps on the Aufnahme confirmation page\n\n* Guard the Aufnahme pages with axe\n\n* Skip the contrast rule in the Aufnahme axe scans\n\nThe Walz brand colours stay below the WCAG contrast minimums by the site\nowner''s decision; every other WCAG A/AA rule stays enforced.\n\n* Send the Aufnahme confirmation once per address\n\n* Keep request bodies and mail error text out of Sentry\n\n* Derive the Aufnahme form''s live checks from the submit''s parse\n\n* Set the Tag, Monat and Jahr labels at label size\n\n* Give the PLZ and Ort errors a full-width row on the Aufnahme form\n\n* Outline the privacy link and submit button clearly on keyboard focus\n\n* Make the email addresses on the Aufnahme pages tappable\n\n* Fit the first Aufnahme input on a phone''s first screen\n\n* Raise the Aufnahme checkbox and radio rows to thumb size\n\n* Keep console output out of Sentry breadcrumbs\n\n* Shorten the Aufnahme form intro\n\n* Drop the Aufnahme loading-state test that repeated the submit test\n\nIt submitted a complete form, costing two Resend sends per run, and only\nasserted what \"submits a complete form\" already covers; the busy state has\nits own test.\n\n* Match the spec to the shorter Aufnahme form intro\n\n* Design the Lernpfad vocabulary for the Aufnahme pages\n\nDirection A from the design exploration: a path rail with section nodes,\nchoice cards, notices, a steps path and a section map, built from tints of\nthe unchanged brand colours.\n\n* Log a fixed line when an Aufnahme email fails to send\n\nResend''s error text can quote a recipient''s address, which would otherwise\nland in the server logs.\n\n* Revise the Lernpfad spec after design and accessibility review\n\nFocus becomes an outline that leaves the state border alone, the date error\nmaps to its section, the spiral ornaments go, and the section map, steps and\nsummary grouping are pinned down.\n\n* Plan the Lernpfad build\n\n* Add the Lernpfad tokens and an outline focus to text inputs\n\n* Work out each Aufnahme form section''s state from the submit rules\n\n* Add path rail, nodes and a steps path to the UI kit\n\n* Add choice cards, choice lists and notices to the UI kit\n\n* Put the Aufnahme form sections on a path\n\nThe four section fieldsets now sit on one continuous rail. Each legend\ncarries a node that shows the section''s status, worked out with the same\nrules the submit uses: from the submitted values before hydration and\nwithout JavaScript, from the form''s own values once mounted. The\nsub-headings get waypoints, the intro shows the next steps as a compact\nsteps path, and the rail ends in a dot beside the submit button, whose\nlabel is now 20px bold. The date row wraps on narrow or zoomed screens.\n\nThe steps path keeps its list role in Safari, and the rail''s end cover\nmoves into the path kit so the form can reuse it.\n\n* Measure PLZ and Ort only after the error summary takes focus\n\nThe test clicked submit without waiting for hydration, so the summary\ncould take focus, and scroll the page, between the four bounding boxes\nit compares. It failed once in a local run. Waiting for the focus first\nmakes every box come from the same scroll position.\n\n* Use choice cards and a notice on the Aufnahme form\n\nBoth \"Wohnt an Ihrer Adresse\" boxes become choice cards and the source\nradios a choice list, with \"Woher genau?\" under \"Anderes\" in the same\nitem; the privacy note becomes a notice with the lock icon. The tints\ncome from :has(), so they follow the controls without JavaScript.\n\nA source row with keyboard focus now gets the card''s outline. The list\nno longer clips, so the outline shows whole, and its end items round\ntheir own corners. The card''s hint no longer overlaps the bottom of its\nlabel, which made a tap there miss the checkbox.\n\n* Group the Aufnahme error summary by section\n\nThe summary lists its links under the section they belong to, in page\norder, with each section''s title as a plain-text label, so the count\nstays its only heading. Errors outside every section close the list in\na group without a label. The grouping uses sectionOf, the function that\nalso decides the section nodes. Focus, the count, the href fallback and\nthe mail variant stay as they were.\n\n* Label the error summary''s groups with the section title alone\n\nThe numbered circles beside the group labels matched nothing on the\npath, where a section with errors shows \"!\" rather than its number. The\nlabel is now the title as plain text, in line with the heading''s text\nand the links.\n\n* Widen the path indent so titles line up with the fields on phones\n\nAt 2rem the 32px node filled the whole indent, so the section titles\nneeded extra padding to clear its ring and sat 8px right of the field\nlabels below them. At 2.5rem the node leaves its own gap, the titles and\nlabels share one left edge, and the phone-only padding goes, in the form\nand in the full steps path alike. The content column at 320px is now\n248px; the date row still fits.\n\n* Move the Aufnahme form''s parts out of the route module\n\nThe sections, the address and date fields and the error summary, with\nthe helpers they share, now live in __formular-parts.tsx, which the\nroute config ignores. The route keeps the loader, the action, the page\nand its hooks. Nothing changes in behaviour; the code moves as it was.\n\n* Match the Lernpfad spec to the 2.5rem path indent\n\n* Show a section map beside the Aufnahme form on wide screens\n\nFrom the lg breakpoint a panel in the site''s right column lists the four\nsections as links on a short path, each node showing the same state as\non the form''s rail. It comes after the form in the DOM and is hidden on\nsmaller screens. The form route moves to the subgrid layout /aufnahme\nuses.\n\nThe e2e helpers that fill section 1 and wait for hydration move to a\nshared module, so the Lernpfad spec can use them too.\n\n* Continue the path on the confirmation page and on /aufnahme\n\n* Ask for the schools attended so far on the Aufnahme form\n\nThe label reads \"Bisher besuchte Schulen\"; the hint now says the list\nstarts after the Volksschule.\n\n* Call the applicant Jugendliche:r on the Aufnahme pages\n\n* Match the specs to the Jugendliche:r wording\n\n* Name the phone menu button for screen readers\n\nThe toggle showed only an icon, so assistive technology announced an\nunnamed button.\n\n* Record the Jugendliche:r decision in the Aufnahme spec\n\n* Ask how parents heard of the Walz in one free-text field\n\nThe radio options and the \"Woher genau?\" field become a single optional\ntextarea. The answer is trimmed, limited to 1000 characters and printed\nin the office email as entered.\n\n* Give every focus mark on the Aufnahme pages the fields'' outline\n\nThe error-summary links and the back link on the confirmation page only\nhad the site''s faint 20% outline. They, the summary itself, the further\nguardian toggle and the existing outlined links now share the fields''\n2px primary-700 outline, and the submit button no longer adds its own\nblue-grey ring on top of it.\n\n* Mark the further guardian toggle with a turning caret\n\nThe plus turned into \"×\" when open, which reads as \"remove this\nperson\" although closing keeps what was typed. The toggle also takes the\nchoice cards'' 12px radius and a 48px minimum height.\n\n* Stop section-map jumps 24px below the top edge\n\nThe jump landed the section flush at the top and clipped its node.\n\n* Show the steps on /aufnahme above the prose as an overview\n\nAfter the four paragraphs they only repeated what was just read.\n\n* Make the phone menu button a 44px target\n\nIt was 32px. The 44px button still fits the logo''s 46px row, so the\nheader keeps its height.\n\n* Point the Lernpfad theme keys at their CSS variables\n\nThe tailwind-merge config reads only the keys, so the values now live\nonce, in app.css. A cn() test proves the inset shadow registration.\n\n* Keep the list role on the error summary''s lists\n\nSafari drops it from a list without bullets.\n\n* Draw the path''s 12px dots with a shared PathDot\n\nThe steps and the end of the form''s path each hand-rolled the same dot.\n\n* Call the applicant the applicant in the form''s test names\n\n* Check the form for sideways overflow at 320px with every reveal open\n\n* Match the Aufnahme specs to the built form\n\nThe source question is one free-text field, the school history asks for\n\"Bisher besuchte Schulen\", the steps on /aufnahme come before the\nprose, and the Lernpfad spec lists the approved copy changes, the\nshared focus outline and PathDot.\n\n* Hang the path in the left margin from xl\n\nFrom 1160px the site''s navigation column leaves room to the left of the\ncontent, so the form''s section rail and the steps on the form, the\nconfirmation page and /aufnahme pull their rail out by the indent. Titles,\nlabels and step texts then share one left edge with the page heading;\nnarrower screens keep the indent. The section map''s rail stays in its panel.\n\n* Describe the hanging path in the Lernpfad spec\n\nPathRail and StepsPath take a hanging prop that puts the rail in the left\nmargin from xl; the Placement section lists the paths that hang and the e2e\nand unit checks that pin the shared left edge.\n\n* Take Agnes''s copy changes on the Aufnahme pages\n\n* Match the specs to Agnes''s copy changes","tree":{"sha":"65463fba005a2eade6f5c9295289c0040a05b155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/65463fba005a2eade6f5c9295289c0040a05b155"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/8d8a29e457c1b796e39ec9f70248b4f891b1c818","verification":{"payload":"tree 65463fba005a2eade6f5c9295289c0040a05b155\nparent a051569484a0ecd043e0f41cafa4ccfd72f90e03\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1791401134 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791401134 +0200\n\nRedesign the Aufnahme form on a Lernpfad design vocabulary (#142)\n\n* Design the Aufnahmeformular redesign\n\nResearch-backed spec for a parent-first, single-page form with structured\naddresses, per-field errors and a confirmation page that explains the next\nsteps. Revised after an independent design and accessibility review.\n\n* Keep exactly one title on the Aufnahme form page\n\n* Plan the Aufnahmeformular redesign implementation\n\n* Validate the Aufnahme form in one shared module\n\n* Add accessible form field primitives and 16px inputs\n\nField and FieldGroup wire hint and error ids into aria-describedby and\naria-invalid. Input and Textarea use 16px text so iOS does not zoom on\nfocus, and draw a 2px border when aria-invalid.\n\nDarken --input and --ring so form controls meet the 3:1 non-text\ncontrast of WCAG 1.4.11 (no dark-mode block exists to update):\n\n  --input  28 5% 90%       -> 28 5% 52%\n    vs --card        1.25 -> 3.68\n    vs --background  1.17 -> 3.44\n  --ring   215 20.2% 65.1% -> 215 20.2% 55%\n    vs --card        2.56 -> 3.60\n    vs --background  2.39 -> 3.36\n\nDeclare WarningCircle in the hand-maintained phosphor type shim.\n\n* Write structured addresses and school history into the Aufnahme email\n\n* Return field errors and send the office copy first from the Aufnahme action\n\n* Rebuild the Aufnahme form parent-first with structured addresses\n\n* Skip the hidden guardian address and describe each date input on the Aufnahme form\n\n* Show per-field errors with a focused summary on the Aufnahme form\n\n* Reword the stale comment in the Aufnahme loading-state test\n\n* Clear emptied optional errors and cover the submit guard reset on the Aufnahme form\n\n* Leave the newsletter box off the Aufnahme form\n\n* Show the next steps on the Aufnahme confirmation page\n\n* Guard the Aufnahme pages with axe\n\n* Skip the contrast rule in the Aufnahme axe scans\n\nThe Walz brand colours stay below the WCAG contrast minimums by the site\nowner''s decision; every other WCAG A/AA rule stays enforced.\n\n* Send the Aufnahme confirmation once per address\n\n* Keep request bodies and mail error text out of Sentry\n\n* Derive the Aufnahme form''s live checks from the submit''s parse\n\n* Set the Tag, Monat and Jahr labels at label size\n\n* Give the PLZ and Ort errors a full-width row on the Aufnahme form\n\n* Outline the privacy link and submit button clearly on keyboard focus\n\n* Make the email addresses on the Aufnahme pages tappable\n\n* Fit the first Aufnahme input on a phone''s first screen\n\n* Raise the Aufnahme checkbox and radio rows to thumb size\n\n* Keep console output out of Sentry breadcrumbs\n\n* Shorten the Aufnahme form intro\n\n* Drop the Aufnahme loading-state test that repeated the submit test\n\nIt submitted a complete form, costing two Resend sends per run, and only\nasserted what \"submits a complete form\" already covers; the busy state has\nits own test.\n\n* Match the spec to the shorter Aufnahme form intro\n\n* Design the Lernpfad vocabulary for the Aufnahme pages\n\nDirection A from the design exploration: a path rail with section nodes,\nchoice cards, notices, a steps path and a section map, built from tints of\nthe unchanged brand colours.\n\n* Log a fixed line when an Aufnahme email fails to send\n\nResend''s error text can quote a recipient''s address, which would otherwise\nland in the server logs.\n\n* Revise the Lernpfad spec after design and accessibility review\n\nFocus becomes an outline that leaves the state border alone, the date error\nmaps to its section, the spiral ornaments go, and the section map, steps and\nsummary grouping are pinned down.\n\n* Plan the Lernpfad build\n\n* Add the Lernpfad tokens and an outline focus to text inputs\n\n* Work out each Aufnahme form section''s state from the submit rules\n\n* Add path rail, nodes and a steps path to the UI kit\n\n* Add choice cards, choice lists and notices to the UI kit\n\n* Put the Aufnahme form sections on a path\n\nThe four section fieldsets now sit on one continuous rail. Each legend\ncarries a node that shows the section''s status, worked out with the same\nrules the submit uses: from the submitted values before hydration and\nwithout JavaScript, from the form''s own values once mounted. The\nsub-headings get waypoints, the intro shows the next steps as a compact\nsteps path, and the rail ends in a dot beside the submit button, whose\nlabel is now 20px bold. The date row wraps on narrow or zoomed screens.\n\nThe steps path keeps its list role in Safari, and the rail''s end cover\nmoves into the path kit so the form can reuse it.\n\n* Measure PLZ and Ort only after the error summary takes focus\n\nThe test clicked submit without waiting for hydration, so the summary\ncould take focus, and scroll the page, between the four bounding boxes\nit compares. It failed once in a local run. Waiting for the focus first\nmakes every box come from the same scroll position.\n\n* Use choice cards and a notice on the Aufnahme form\n\nBoth \"Wohnt an Ihrer Adresse\" boxes become choice cards and the source\nradios a choice list, with \"Woher genau?\" under \"Anderes\" in the same\nitem; the privacy note becomes a notice with the lock icon. The tints\ncome from :has(), so they follow the controls without JavaScript.\n\nA source row with keyboard focus now gets the card''s outline. The list\nno longer clips, so the outline shows whole, and its end items round\ntheir own corners. The card''s hint no longer overlaps the bottom of its\nlabel, which made a tap there miss the checkbox.\n\n* Group the Aufnahme error summary by section\n\nThe summary lists its links under the section they belong to, in page\norder, with each section''s title as a plain-text label, so the count\nstays its only heading. Errors outside every section close the list in\na group without a label. The grouping uses sectionOf, the function that\nalso decides the section nodes. Focus, the count, the href fallback and\nthe mail variant stay as they were.\n\n* Label the error summary''s groups with the section title alone\n\nThe numbered circles beside the group labels matched nothing on the\npath, where a section with errors shows \"!\" rather than its number. The\nlabel is now the title as plain text, in line with the heading''s text\nand the links.\n\n* Widen the path indent so titles line up with the fields on phones\n\nAt 2rem the 32px node filled the whole indent, so the section titles\nneeded extra padding to clear its ring and sat 8px right of the field\nlabels below them. At 2.5rem the node leaves its own gap, the titles and\nlabels share one left edge, and the phone-only padding goes, in the form\nand in the full steps path alike. The content column at 320px is now\n248px; the date row still fits.\n\n* Move the Aufnahme form''s parts out of the route module\n\nThe sections, the address and date fields and the error summary, with\nthe helpers they share, now live in __formular-parts.tsx, which the\nroute config ignores. The route keeps the loader, the action, the page\nand its hooks. Nothing changes in behaviour; the code moves as it was.\n\n* Match the Lernpfad spec to the 2.5rem path indent\n\n* Show a section map beside the Aufnahme form on wide screens\n\nFrom the lg breakpoint a panel in the site''s right column lists the four\nsections as links on a short path, each node showing the same state as\non the form''s rail. It comes after the form in the DOM and is hidden on\nsmaller screens. The form route moves to the subgrid layout /aufnahme\nuses.\n\nThe e2e helpers that fill section 1 and wait for hydration move to a\nshared module, so the Lernpfad spec can use them too.\n\n* Continue the path on the confirmation page and on /aufnahme\n\n* Ask for the schools attended so far on the Aufnahme form\n\nThe label reads \"Bisher besuchte Schulen\"; the hint now says the list\nstarts after the Volksschule.\n\n* Call the applicant Jugendliche:r on the Aufnahme pages\n\n* Match the specs to the Jugendliche:r wording\n\n* Name the phone menu button for screen readers\n\nThe toggle showed only an icon, so assistive technology announced an\nunnamed button.\n\n* Record the Jugendliche:r decision in the Aufnahme spec\n\n* Ask how parents heard of the Walz in one free-text field\n\nThe radio options and the \"Woher genau?\" field become a single optional\ntextarea. The answer is trimmed, limited to 1000 characters and printed\nin the office email as entered.\n\n* Give every focus mark on the Aufnahme pages the fields'' outline\n\nThe error-summary links and the back link on the confirmation page only\nhad the site''s faint 20% outline. They, the summary itself, the further\nguardian toggle and the existing outlined links now share the fields''\n2px primary-700 outline, and the submit button no longer adds its own\nblue-grey ring on top of it.\n\n* Mark the further guardian toggle with a turning caret\n\nThe plus turned into \"×\" when open, which reads as \"remove this\nperson\" although closing keeps what was typed. The toggle also takes the\nchoice cards'' 12px radius and a 48px minimum height.\n\n* Stop section-map jumps 24px below the top edge\n\nThe jump landed the section flush at the top and clipped its node.\n\n* Show the steps on /aufnahme above the prose as an overview\n\nAfter the four paragraphs they only repeated what was just read.\n\n* Make the phone menu button a 44px target\n\nIt was 32px. The 44px button still fits the logo''s 46px row, so the\nheader keeps its height.\n\n* Point the Lernpfad theme keys at their CSS variables\n\nThe tailwind-merge config reads only the keys, so the values now live\nonce, in app.css. A cn() test proves the inset shadow registration.\n\n* Keep the list role on the error summary''s lists\n\nSafari drops it from a list without bullets.\n\n* Draw the path''s 12px dots with a shared PathDot\n\nThe steps and the end of the form''s path each hand-rolled the same dot.\n\n* Call the applicant the applicant in the form''s test names\n\n* Check the form for sideways overflow at 320px with every reveal open\n\n* Match the Aufnahme specs to the built form\n\nThe source question is one free-text field, the school history asks for\n\"Bisher besuchte Schulen\", the steps on /aufnahme come before the\nprose, and the Lernpfad spec lists the approved copy changes, the\nshared focus outline and PathDot.\n\n* Hang the path in the left margin from xl\n\nFrom 1160px the site''s navigation column leaves room to the left of the\ncontent, so the form''s section rail and the steps on the form, the\nconfirmation page and /aufnahme pull their rail out by the indent. Titles,\nlabels and step texts then share one left edge with the page heading;\nnarrower screens keep the indent. The section map''s rail stays in its panel.\n\n* Describe the hanging path in the Lernpfad spec\n\nPathRail and StepsPath take a hanging prop that puts the rail in the left\nmargin from xl; the Placement section lists the paths that hang and the e2e\nand unit checks that pin the shared left edge.\n\n* Take Agnes''s copy changes on the Aufnahme pages\n\n* Match the specs to Agnes''s copy changes","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxpyuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAw58QAHf4HrqTTeq45WbKdm1mcTgt\n3valn8QvvTL8oYbKHvuBpXpjOxHQK3LdzogbNG8pKFCw5KXrKxlRRkTmgr3jgAQb\n/tJy1ev2K6rZ6alpyayDGp98yzwB8F0cJ/eYFJdhYri+Asom6kiJmdB2AY5S5Ja/\n1UHFjUBZHqKX1BplRsk6pUhqabXAIZomXnorXIFfLHCNclsEfIALZSkNibdFSazd\nztteEQ4L2BGbixTfBYLqp0sxu7j90of4jHSKTRKx8RZbimOr4qF2+04jzn2AyK9z\nS55kTapMsjniWIrb6dyyulyn0hzHX6ZuzQPRrGEG7EYph6CMK2AQbEvbM1T9fekw\nIVFMDxKhvFAqAujzlpzvyZj5bZdq+M/klReKBSxvrLGforKxOVQF4EplepYdg3mQ\nWDRKYDni9FuUBy96btP04AvDa7RvDs14GkF8xGQzDLDIkHhTJqvOwkarO7iM0ba4\noYO+ihpcHEt83iwMbd1thOV1b2wWLBuPI/uM8Kb3FbBuNNP1h7Bd39laftcvtl32\nL1xYRt3lB9X1smnhfIJjs2T8U/aVFzQlZWSZI1ipdj63kUr3l/CfJ2cqWZyYj+E9\nVXY+toBPd/kVLn6Jo1h6DXd0z95EV4urvvtJ1JBMiWjRhPg9FuYQosx6LQBmcSNj\nh5XXsDqKMZmVVf4zwwon\n=SVuw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T19:25:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/8d8a29e457c1b796e39ec9f70248b4f891b1c818","node_id":"C_kwDOKP_7ZtoAKDhkOGEyOWU0NTdjMWI3OTZlMzllYzlmNzAyNDhiNGY4OTFiMWM4MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/a051569484a0ecd043e0f41cafa4ccfd72f90e03","sha":"a051569484a0ecd043e0f41cafa4ccfd72f90e03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/a051569484a0ecd043e0f41cafa4ccfd72f90e03"}],"sha":"8d8a29e457c1b796e39ec9f70248b4f891b1c818","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/8d8a29e457c1b796e39ec9f70248b4f891b1c818"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340520?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis","id":340520,"login":"ferdinandsalis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDUyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/a051569484a0ecd043e0f41cafa4ccfd72f90e03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:57:04Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:57:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Key the event rows on /aktuelles (#141)\n\nEach event row in the Schuljahr list is an unkeyed fragment (the\n\"next event\" divider plus the AccordionItem), so every render of\n/aktuelles logged React''s \"Each child in a list should have a unique\nkey prop\" warning, visible in the dev server output of every CI\nPlaywright run. The key on AccordionItem does not count; the fragment\nitself needs one. It is now a Fragment keyed by the event''s Sanity _id.\n\nThe new unit test renders the route through a routes stub and fails on\nany console error, including this warning.","tree":{"sha":"9e3ff22a13d5f00fa915ed77a09e1819d075778c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/9e3ff22a13d5f00fa915ed77a09e1819d075778c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/a051569484a0ecd043e0f41cafa4ccfd72f90e03","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e3ff22a13d5f00fa915ed77a09e1819d075778c\nparent 1d5f3bef2e7d5db05fc893aeaa71084d10315f97\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1790769424 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790769424 +0200\n\nKey the event rows on /aktuelles (#141)\n\nEach event row in the Schuljahr list is an unkeyed fragment (the\n\"next event\" divider plus the AccordionItem), so every render of\n/aktuelles logged React''s \"Each child in a list should have a unique\nkey prop\" warning, visible in the dev server output of every CI\nPlaywright run. The key on AccordionItem does not count; the fragment\nitself needs one. It is now a Fragment keyed by the event''s Sanity _id.\n\nThe new unit test renders the route through a routes stub and fails on\nany console error, including this warning.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPkQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgSAQAFef6xs2RtpIjQ/R/fIrBRk7\nzoAwEqUNIB1SJ17au07RbPHHC6y0y9NiwPX/968RuYHHMk67Zo93Yq+UxI9R9x3U\nvmMs2VxLbPi+HSQrDQu50ccO92F3+yC5Q7VwqXa/H5Sv7cF8IjNn9XEP6N8ATv11\nfMoKmWvrnbh8W+d89+lJVEijhRCafdJ/6AauD61dQmUlcIFpe7S6AjH+/ftd0AmN\n2sfGzUy52mZnXmFy33/s91tz5aRzOIQlEWmwsdDLIogLLUSQhdTO3Im3xNEIorxO\nH/CfK9LT7ecDJfLqRa4RQclnkx0TtaUXDOlhAz8v6JXiFDakYRJ3GzcPigai4Xgp\nYETPdeKw++XE0J1RathEc4pBdHHPCxVRBCxnNvb4yNEvbbDPVKY2n8Yn+U5vJ9DN\nVqc29jr+9W8/0ZzgE1iN/Qm+xWEnXtsJ4mKwJjbauqRdfrvLZyVuFAa6IGGVbKKY\nEFlEE5JEHM9eHELzz4u8EaqOm908PrA10pQ81vXPc4UV0YTuIPRZFaSK0aEuQGL2\nKmNQMSn/MGIzSD8mvZGHHfNvfQ9JbCoLEXta1hM7XG6c95/bFNzn4R3/OfVn3VQZ\n4se7zjlNfFfECc5GYHgevWTINIL/Je6wtZ9zLigWoho4Z9y8LnsbasN5UPLd92uX\nDBXYNaHyQnHLMAHVUiTI\n=BQyL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:57:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/a051569484a0ecd043e0f41cafa4ccfd72f90e03","node_id":"C_kwDOKP_7ZtoAKGEwNTE1Njk0ODRhMGVjZDA0M2UwZjQxY2FmYTRjY2ZkNzJmOTBlMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/1d5f3bef2e7d5db05fc893aeaa71084d10315f97","sha":"1d5f3bef2e7d5db05fc893aeaa71084d10315f97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/1d5f3bef2e7d5db05fc893aeaa71084d10315f97"}],"sha":"a051569484a0ecd043e0f41cafa4ccfd72f90e03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/a051569484a0ecd043e0f41cafa4ccfd72f90e03"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340520?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis","id":340520,"login":"ferdinandsalis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDUyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/1d5f3bef2e7d5db05fc893aeaa71084d10315f97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:56:48Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:56:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Keep Aufnahme test submissions out of the school inbox (#135)\n\nEvery e2e run submits the Anmeldeformular three times. With the real\nResend key, which walz/mise.toml exports into every worktree, each\nsubmission mailed office@walz.at and sent confirmations to example.com\naddresses that bounce. A run of ~25 local suites flooded the office.\n\nOutside production the school''s copy now goes to Resend''s test inbox,\nand the e2e data uses delivered+…@resend.dev, which Resend accepts\nwithout harming the domain''s reputation.\n\nResend also never throws on a rejected send; it returns { error },\nwhich we ignored. A family could see \"Danke\" while no mail went out,\nand CI''s submit tests passed on a placeholder key without sending.\nBoth sends now surface that error, so CI needs a real RESEND_API_KEY\nin the test environment.","tree":{"sha":"f17615bddbcc00864bcbeaaa5337c75b4e7a3435","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/f17615bddbcc00864bcbeaaa5337c75b4e7a3435"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/1d5f3bef2e7d5db05fc893aeaa71084d10315f97","verification":{"payload":"tree f17615bddbcc00864bcbeaaa5337c75b4e7a3435\nparent 0d17a1b98b05b749d8071eeef23f65987e3ec85a\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1790769408 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790769408 +0200\n\nKeep Aufnahme test submissions out of the school inbox (#135)\n\nEvery e2e run submits the Anmeldeformular three times. With the real\nResend key, which walz/mise.toml exports into every worktree, each\nsubmission mailed office@walz.at and sent confirmations to example.com\naddresses that bounce. A run of ~25 local suites flooded the office.\n\nOutside production the school''s copy now goes to Resend''s test inbox,\nand the e2e data uses delivered+…@resend.dev, which Resend accepts\nwithout harming the domain''s reputation.\n\nResend also never throws on a rejected send; it returns { error },\nwhich we ignored. A family could see \"Danke\" while no mail went out,\nand CI''s submit tests passed on a placeholder key without sending.\nBoth sends now surface that error, so CI needs a real RESEND_API_KEY\nin the test environment.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPkACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAui0QAFHTCvRlIo9wa7mmi3cFn7nz\nN0cf3KARxtCm7kmnTs018jxwKnUdtbibb7R+txn+x+8q1rcFll83txh/QkXU8xWh\nPzPsrB+nfbqPzDZpcg4FvJHT4x3gQtcWsMVnekr3B82QJTswW6v4lSsE6ro0KxUz\nJwkeaLA7/ET7e+HHlhTQZpt2LBTDAlTxWVGvWNc/agGK3w6pR9NFTobIXbXHgxCa\nybgVDHQd3Audn0PTn0eMmcy/lU94KtMWuzSnhIJaKsXt9QyoTPHdZXGdWRMm8BXH\n+M8H60pwt+ai+39M7MthWc6sdNYaU8BvENKIP15VpU0snporIn6NIywH0J7XSGt+\nu8ty/3sLJ84j1kPaSEDwrgTpD9uoIVjPinV+JHej4wa7KieXLMtvEiFPh96oK+kx\nYP68w+8PCwrfETNv8X20w6Q6Y8n+0Nz4vIbZT/Wz2q2ppm5tQ4uNG+KV/mSUAWxK\nJvwWnSL4MqaLHnYCQOWa0CMCsuOLxmgR9fJq5DgIsf9alfRGFDvrTbWDfOINLKsY\ndLQdRo6q2SRlPEq8yRsrIPN7RNaSeqLbFyD4z6dkGO+QV/PmeUTOdoj20wmVajHS\n1VSWO/fYXMxF5EbsuHG8Hs7Di4J0K69r/P+2Fbj+v/bAyBmHARvRFz6Ct/G8tFxW\nB/7m9vwV7HisMOiva1bp\n=MO10\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:56:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/1d5f3bef2e7d5db05fc893aeaa71084d10315f97","node_id":"C_kwDOKP_7ZtoAKDFkNWYzYmVmMmU3ZDVkYjA1ZmM4OTNhZWFhNzEwODRkMTAzMTVmOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/0d17a1b98b05b749d8071eeef23f65987e3ec85a","sha":"0d17a1b98b05b749d8071eeef23f65987e3ec85a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/0d17a1b98b05b749d8071eeef23f65987e3ec85a"}],"sha":"1d5f3bef2e7d5db05fc893aeaa71084d10315f97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/1d5f3bef2e7d5db05fc893aeaa71084d10315f97"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340520?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis","id":340520,"login":"ferdinandsalis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDUyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/0d17a1b98b05b749d8071eeef23f65987e3ec85a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:56:39Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:56:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Regenerate Sanity types and load event attachments (#140)\n\n* Regenerate the Sanity schema and query types\n\nThe committed schema.json predated the costs, curriculum, event,\nhome-shoutout, schoolYear and project documents, so most generated\nquery results were null or Array<never>. Regenerated with\n`sanity schema extract` and `sanity typegen generate` against the\ncurrent queries.\n\nPerson slugs are now typed as Sanity''s Slug, whose `current` is\noptional; StaffCard already reads it with optional chaining.\n\n* Load event attachments on Termine pages\n\n`attachments { … }` projects the array as a single object and always\nyields null, so /termine/<slug> never listed an event''s files. The\narray traversal `attachments[] { … }` resolves each file to its URL.\nThe Aktuelles query had the same projection and gets the same fix.\n\nThe tests run both queries through groq-js, Sanity''s reference GROQ\nengine (already installed via @sanity/codegen, now declared), and\nparse the result with EventSchema like the routes do.\n\n* Use the generated type for the home shoutout\n\nThe hand-written assertion stood in for the generated HomeQueryResult,\nwhich typed the shoutout as null until the schema was re-extracted. Every\nuse is guarded by a truthiness check, so the nullable generated fields\ntypecheck as they are.","tree":{"sha":"31c435f2eb1a5a0831e61e956ea29d55eacccf44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/31c435f2eb1a5a0831e61e956ea29d55eacccf44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/0d17a1b98b05b749d8071eeef23f65987e3ec85a","verification":{"payload":"tree 31c435f2eb1a5a0831e61e956ea29d55eacccf44\nparent 0db07a10b41d1ebaedd49164cca1a7670f6c387b\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1790769399 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790769399 +0200\n\nRegenerate Sanity types and load event attachments (#140)\n\n* Regenerate the Sanity schema and query types\n\nThe committed schema.json predated the costs, curriculum, event,\nhome-shoutout, schoolYear and project documents, so most generated\nquery results were null or Array<never>. Regenerated with\n`sanity schema extract` and `sanity typegen generate` against the\ncurrent queries.\n\nPerson slugs are now typed as Sanity''s Slug, whose `current` is\noptional; StaffCard already reads it with optional chaining.\n\n* Load event attachments on Termine pages\n\n`attachments { … }` projects the array as a single object and always\nyields null, so /termine/<slug> never listed an event''s files. The\narray traversal `attachments[] { … }` resolves each file to its URL.\nThe Aktuelles query had the same projection and gets the same fix.\n\nThe tests run both queries through groq-js, Sanity''s reference GROQ\nengine (already installed via @sanity/codegen, now declared), and\nparse the result with EventSchema like the routes do.\n\n* Use the generated type for the home shoutout\n\nThe hand-written assertion stood in for the generated HomeQueryResult,\nwhich typed the shoutout as null until the schema was re-extracted. Every\nuse is guarded by a truthiness check, so the nullable generated fields\ntypecheck as they are.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPj3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfWoQAAEA2L7f+VA5NtIkXayK2DDv\nkMBc6UfYSNJS5oOGGkyJjSCswgYf0acl1vAl0325UlOwxyN45DMHRCiiuOtVLgUz\nQRINGM12YXz2PXj+EEYbGDrqkN2Ve3uc+aiSlzCqznabrvckbETMKznm1wi8N1kN\nTFgP9XRbTpS+h0V7IwukBIHUmY62/VwAiOFlPuSGAO+I+uaf7M5Motddjk5xYeCM\nKta9TJvNQdk8foKVcHHrPhVqzDQekGk8lARk30g+CJQfPGr2lLecGnwZELVQcnPb\noRpkHFlAItsd2tzaKTtvIS6rZXBJNDyFZVYJ/Ld7Jv+GINMUqRaOHjaVhRYy2yyR\nCEoeYUBKIkyMAj51vlKsm