hub.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/77500e8d7b574c6e8ed6cdbd51e6ff075cc0e40a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:45:32Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:45:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Start e2e tests only once the dev server renders a page (#138)\n\nThe dev server''s first request loads the server build, compiling every\nroute module for SSR. On the CI runner that takes about 20s, longer than\nthe 15s test timeout, so the first test (page.goto(''/aufnahme'')) failed\nand passed on retry: the one flaky test in every run. It is not the\nstartup dependency pre-bundle: with no bundling at all, the first\nrequest still takes ~8s locally and took 17.6s on CI.\n\nPlaywright now polls GET / instead of the port, so tests start against a\nwarm server, and the webServer timeout is 120s to cover the cold start\non slow runners.","tree":{"sha":"64d29e3ebc9edc00f43584b6c9920e55a1d1e62b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/64d29e3ebc9edc00f43584b6c9920e55a1d1e62b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/77500e8d7b574c6e8ed6cdbd51e6ff075cc0e40a","verification":{"payload":"tree 64d29e3ebc9edc00f43584b6c9920e55a1d1e62b\nparent 741b7dcc98bc197d5bccc19b57b543704bc138e3\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1790768732 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790768732 +0200\n\nStart e2e tests only once the dev server renders a page (#138)\n\nThe dev server''s first request loads the server build, compiling every\nroute module for SSR. On the CI runner that takes about 20s, longer than\nthe 15s test timeout, so the first test (page.goto(''/aufnahme'')) failed\nand passed on retry: the one flaky test in every run. It is not the\nstartup dependency pre-bundle: with no bundling at all, the first\nrequest still takes ~8s locally and took 17.6s on CI.\n\nPlaywright now polls GET / instead of the port, so tests start against a\nwarm server, and the webServer timeout is 120s to cover the cold start\non slow runners.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPZcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1GkQAJxdy7lmPBsJPZyGLGIQYiIT\nRZ0EYWMXBKgk2inbYE4jYJhzV73/2qXIceISM/8IyiTM1uPm8bYa94j8lYYu1qGO\nPlCb+jkUJoltwWD3WSb2/jyoi5uAojPN7GKkvcOhqiUPma5wQbSRm4BXuh9NiMQy\naoqos1q3rvwyrFgqaNdaC+ZBljxjTVLjyFhIv8OQBpai4rNI3nzKsMDq9L4Es4kh\nRjWaXJTkKqtqUXgyJ91MdJG2XhfFVacuohM38ifX+JhISejn58hh/Uo6G+la6oDt\nesMEiiPOJsLu4ZRY3/vKzboz7d2CJMbEIS85NbJSql2ML3LW4ad2ZyBKB1rDIZLU\nrwvzxaEJuPZAbj2JH3xgZBS95YEIkyx/u6vrCLDWzrss622FlBNNcCC2udOmo2Bo\nfUkrr/zDTjZnaWjHsg3xSZqD5upYQNg7UsGPWdDMKZ/RupMG6LqM/15qFGhAYr0R\njuwmR0tePdgXFhenr0zJO5Yr2hCti0D4t5Qobn4+1QkfWUL7Hp/vck1b02coT8Nd\nWelplJqT9Q7MgdNVGjkc9jyeYHZQ68exgpicEE9f6WlJH89YLYWpFmm6vFGqF68F\nZX22MCePntSzav5wYP9TAUUoN/HnYFfomzONEMKidwwU0mZK6OHHnItufu14to2q\nuGJzypOoJQ3yZ0uTmAMT\n=J+S5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:45:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/77500e8d7b574c6e8ed6cdbd51e6ff075cc0e40a","node_id":"C_kwDOKP_7ZtoAKDc3NTAwZThkN2I1NzRjNmU4ZWQ2Y2RiZDUxZTZmZjA3NWNjMGU0MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/741b7dcc98bc197d5bccc19b57b543704bc138e3","sha":"741b7dcc98bc197d5bccc19b57b543704bc138e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/741b7dcc98bc197d5bccc19b57b543704bc138e3"}],"sha":"77500e8d7b574c6e8ed6cdbd51e6ff075cc0e40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/77500e8d7b574c6e8ed6cdbd51e6ff075cc0e40a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340520?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis","id":340520,"login":"ferdinandsalis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDUyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/741b7dcc98bc197d5bccc19b57b543704bc138e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:31:50Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:31:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Upgrade Sanity Studio to 6.17 (#137)\n\nsanity, @sanity/vision and groq move to 6.17.0 (@sanity/cli 8.13.0).\nThat clears the 5 audit findings on main: adm-zip under\n@sanity/runtime-cli now resolves to 0.6.1, and markdown-it left with\n@portabletext/editor 6.\n\n@sanity/cli 8 brings its own exact pins, all CLI-only, so three\noverrides get npm audit to 0:\n- @module-federation/dts-plugin 2.9.0 (via @sanity/workbench-cli) pins\n  adm-zip 0.6.0 and undici 7.29.0; the undici pin also got hoisted and\n  downgraded jsdom''s copy.\n- @vercel/frameworks 3.29.0 pins smol-toml 1.5.2 (GHSA-7w5x-hrqm-74c2).\nDrop them once @sanity/cli stops pinning these versions. The\n@sanity/uuid override is gone: @sanity/uuid 3.0.3 declares uuid ^11\nitself, and the lockfile is identical without it.\n\nCompanion bumps within existing ranges: @sanity/orderable-document-list\n2.0.25 (@sanity/ui 4, so the Studio has one @sanity/ui and one theme\ncontext), @sanity/client 7.27.0 and react/react-dom 19.2.8, which new\npeers of sanity 6 require. loader.server.ts no longer casts to\nsanity''s SanityClient, which is now @sanity/client 8''s type.\n\nThe typegen config moves from sanity-typegen.json into sanity.cli.ts,\nas @sanity/cli 8 asks; the generated types are byte-identical. Studio\nsearch now uses the groq2024 strategy (the v6 default).\n\nSanity 6''s global CSS reset (@layer sui.global) reaches /studio only;\nthe isolation test now also checks that /studio does carry it.","tree":{"sha":"65c00637956d272002b22196c348ce4a3a67e8d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/65c00637956d272002b22196c348ce4a3a67e8d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/741b7dcc98bc197d5bccc19b57b543704bc138e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 65c00637956d272002b22196c348ce4a3a67e8d6\nparent b54f225456843c9a90230543f327ba114bd994d1\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1790767910 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790767910 +0200\n\nUpgrade Sanity Studio to 6.17 (#137)\n\nsanity, @sanity/vision and groq move to 6.17.0 (@sanity/cli 8.13.0).\nThat clears the 5 audit findings on main: adm-zip under\n@sanity/runtime-cli now resolves to 0.6.1, and markdown-it left with\n@portabletext/editor 6.\n\n@sanity/cli 8 brings its own exact pins, all CLI-only, so three\noverrides get npm audit to 0:\n- @module-federation/dts-plugin 2.9.0 (via @sanity/workbench-cli) pins\n  adm-zip 0.6.0 and undici 7.29.0; the undici pin also got hoisted and\n  downgraded jsdom''s copy.\n- @vercel/frameworks 3.29.0 pins smol-toml 1.5.2 (GHSA-7w5x-hrqm-74c2).\nDrop them once @sanity/cli stops pinning these versions. The\n@sanity/uuid override is gone: @sanity/uuid 3.0.3 declares uuid ^11\nitself, and the lockfile is identical without it.\n\nCompanion bumps within existing ranges: @sanity/orderable-document-list\n2.0.25 (@sanity/ui 4, so the Studio has one @sanity/ui and one theme\ncontext), @sanity/client 7.27.0 and react/react-dom 19.2.8, which new\npeers of sanity 6 require. loader.server.ts no longer casts to\nsanity''s SanityClient, which is now @sanity/client 8''s type.\n\nThe typegen config moves from sanity-typegen.json into sanity.cli.ts,\nas @sanity/cli 8 asks; the generated types are byte-identical. Studio\nsearch now uses the groq2024 strategy (the v6 default).\n\nSanity 6''s global CSS reset (@layer sui.global) reaches /studio only;\nthe isolation test now also checks that /studio does carry it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPMnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5c4QAEY0WLi/+AuzSZRt75BPBzbL\nqpOpcODrnrgkffks2DlOYyDhMPqiIHp4eNffaNOLWiqfI5Pv5OOGYLMLLO0hAT7P\nyXLrFlBbxi5dT1DkYeQ39s6hRCb1MoXJkbyaVwKvyoL3QZRiScysLnRO8OsZS5SM\nlM02jmfvNeORLJwENSCjtMUFfqWC2sRBw0zPzTMvt4IlJvQrOdbvmXJ3CHRr