97d5bccc19b57b543704bc138e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/741b7dcc98bc197d5bccc19b57b543704bc138e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340520?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis","id":340520,"login":"ferdinandsalis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDUyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/b54f225456843c9a90230543f327ba114bd994d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:31:05Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:31:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop shipping Sanity Studio to public pages (#136)\n\nPublic routes parsed query results with zod read-models that lived in\nthe Studio schema files, so importing EventSchema or alphabetMap pulled\nthe whole `sanity` package into the client: nine public routes loaded\na 4.5 MB chunk (1.4 MB gzipped). The read-models now live in\napp/sanity/models, which never imports `sanity`; the schema files\nimport from there. The moved code is unchanged. Public route JS drops\nto 150-340 KB. The new e2e test fails if a public page requests the\n`sanity` package or carries Sanity''s CSS layers, which sanity 6 adds as\na global reset that outranks Tailwind.\n\nReact Router''s future.unstable_optimizeDeps makes the dev server crawl\nall routes for client dependencies at startup. Without it Vite\ndiscovered them page by page and re-bundled mid-session, breaking pages\nmid-navigation (two React copies); CI hid this behind retries, with 2\nflaky tests on every main run. The production build is unchanged apart\nfrom the serialized flag.\n\nAlso adds the Sanity 6 upgrade plan (docs/plans/2026-09-30-sanity-6-upgrade.md).","tree":{"sha":"912ac6cadaa46749abbe368bb0a7ed03e241fa6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/912ac6cadaa46749abbe368bb0a7ed03e241fa6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/b54f225456843c9a90230543f327ba114bd994d1","verification":{"payload":"tree 912ac6cadaa46749abbe368bb0a7ed03e241fa6d\nparent fd42e7d447487eae62b5312a6136f2ec30711652\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1790767865 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790767865 +0200\n\nStop shipping Sanity Studio to public pages (#136)\n\nPublic routes parsed query results with zod read-models that lived in\nthe Studio schema files, so importing EventSchema or alphabetMap pulled\nthe whole `sanity` package into the client: nine public routes loaded\na 4.5 MB chunk (1.4 MB gzipped). The read-models now live in\napp/sanity/models, which never imports `sanity`; the schema files\nimport from there. The moved code is unchanged. Public route JS drops\nto 150-340 KB. The new e2e test fails if a public page requests the\n`sanity` package or carries Sanity''s CSS layers, which sanity 6 adds as\na global reset that outranks Tailwind.\n\nReact Router''s future.unstable_optimizeDeps makes the dev server crawl\nall routes for client dependencies at startup. Without it Vite\ndiscovered them page by page and re-bundled mid-session, breaking pages\nmid-navigation (two React copies); CI hid this behind retries, with 2\nflaky tests on every main run. The production build is unchanged apart\nfrom the serialized flag.\n\nAlso adds the Sanity 6 upgrade plan (docs/plans/2026-09-30-sanity-6-upgrade.md).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPL5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATkYQAA7afS9y1kHJux677d7nmy2m\nxooCCwdJX6I8UOZ+Qny5jcV/jsFPS+DsK3PdVhtdHWtipF+2KhF0qHOHLjMsg0h+\nDn86ChkQhi82ttnrFVaRC67CutlKDaVNrj6AsKJ900cBbf6K/sxyH2zTFDKZesZo\njyz9D4Egxuvqfis1gNxfb0groFhWGCo3QiJXAWJyQD9lLL4c32X60Bv8vWBsrvgM\n5QBcG+nHy7Lhuj0veh/DIpF0M+QY0xgNFbmksNGMvIgutyyQkDuKnRS3csKY8U/B\nA3fXLE9ItpduH43Fwoi165cVQhvaKPJ9Yvuhbyn+hCujBwcEKCVyhvGgn4uMMQWo\nZRyWVq8xKYY9DZGMcnve8lLBvq1NUhB2DgO7CpT6PkCungdl2+3bbNAInycYEjwr\nxp08uovOi9nnffdKAIuzEPDXIJ+VAnHBeuysk/rZvs9C3+9pLPRbUdvAMahsJvuj\nyuTMJnsbf+2rCs88kG4gMY5FSoRyAdlM1qh+5WjEjPVUXj7TaXT03tI0i4H+toI0\ntBNAsN2SJfkhqtug+YBZAXN+ts8BHKxFSBxw6sYks24RfPlgC1wqJR1G2acpmhqQ\nmA++UQrlNCX8fucPwk4CKll8w7AbrFGjoqXjgsLzxfE7Arp3Tc1cznFS95jdQlvZ\ns4ZWUO74XA4G5FrACiv6\n=4fh5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:31:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/b54f225456843c9a90230543f327ba114bd994d1","node_id":"C_kwDOKP_7ZtoAKGI1NGYyMjU0NTY4NDNjOWE5MDIzMDU0M2YzMjdiYTExNGJkOTk0ZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/fd42e7d447487eae62b5312a6136f2ec30711652","sha":"fd42e7d447487eae62b5312a6136f2ec30711652","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/fd42e7d447487eae62b5312a6136f2ec30711652"}],"sha":"b54f225456843c9a90230543f327ba114bd994d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/b54f225456843c9a90230543f327ba114bd994d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340520?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis","id":340520,"login":"ferdinandsalis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDUyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/fd42e7d447487eae62b5312a6136f2ec30711652/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T05:56:13Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T05:56:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Resolve 26 of 30 npm audit findings with in-range updates (#134)\n\n`npm audit fix` (no --force), plus lockstep bumps for packages that\npeer on an exact version, which legacy-peer-deps would otherwise hide:\n\n- react-router 7.17.0 -> 7.18.4 (open redirect, route-matching DoS,\n  SSR constructor injection). All @react-router/* packages move with it\n  because @react-router/node and /express peer on react-router exactly.\n- vitest and @vitest/coverage-v8 4.1.8 -> 4.1.11 (coverage-v8 peers on\n  vitest exactly).\n- Server runtime: body-parser and qs (express), ip-address\n  (express-rate-limit), morgan, @opentelemetry/* 2.11.0 (Sentry).\n- Studio and CLI transitives under sanity: tar, undici, dompurify,\n  linkify-it, nanoid, form-data, smol-toml, postcss, brace-expansion.\n- Raise the js-yaml override floor to ^3.15.2: @vercel/frameworks still\n  pins js-yaml 3.13.1 exactly, and 3.14.x is affected by new advisories.\n- Nested vite 7.3.5 -> 7.3.6 under the Sanity CLI packages and\n  vite-node. 7.3.6 accepts esbuild ^0.28, so their vulnerable esbuild\n  0.27.7 copies dedupe to the root esbuild 0.28.2. audit fix does not do\n  this itself because vite is not the vulnerable package.\n\nStill open: adm-zip <0.6.1 via sanity''s @sanity/runtime-cli, which is\nonly fixed through sanity 6.","tree":{"sha":"b06dc6d86a85627536548f08837cf086d83e021c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/b06dc6d86a85627536548f08837cf086d83e021c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/fd42e7d447487eae62b5312a6136f2ec30711652","verification":{"payload":"tree b06dc6d86a85627536548f08837cf086d83e021c\nparent a25c0fe206a6c0f4bc549cb2d847accc903e7462\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1790747773 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790747773 +0200\n\nResolve 26 of 30 npm audit findings with in-range updates (#134)\n\n`npm audit fix` (no --force), plus lockstep bumps for packages that\npeer on an exact version, which legacy-peer-deps would otherwise hide:\n\n- react-router 7.17.0 -> 7.18.4 (open redirect, route-matching DoS,\n  SSR constructor injection). All @react-router/* packages move with it\n  because @react-router/node and /express peer on react-router exactly.\n- vitest and @vitest/coverage-v8 4.1.8 -> 4.1.11 (coverage-v8 peers on\n  vitest exactly).\n- Server runtime: body-parser and qs (express), ip-address\n  (express-rate-limit), morgan, @opentelemetry/* 2.11.0 (Sentry).\n- Studio and CLI transitives under sanity: tar, undici, dompurify,\n  linkify-it, nanoid, form-data, smol-toml, postcss, brace-expansion.\n- Raise the js-yaml override floor to ^3.15.2: @vercel/frameworks still\n  pins js-yaml 3.13.1 exactly, and 3.14.x is affected by new advisories.\n- Nested vite 7.3.5 -> 7.3.6 under the Sanity CLI packages and\n  vite-node. 7.3.6 accepts esbuild ^0.28, so their vulnerable esbuild\n  0.27.7 copies dedupe to the root esbuild 0.28.2. audit fix does not do\n  this itself because vite is not the vulnerable package.\n\nStill open: adm-zip <0.6.1 via sanity''s @sanity/runtime-cli, which is\nonly fixed through sanity 6.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvKR9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABQwQAGzbT19sprQwqU/6SnScbpYm\nOnNhzVb6qPV//0Q/o0Az8uUyxuRpxJPB3+09hDAiRGCG+m3xe+fAsNap59xoqnT3\nyzSfpchZaikwE3HLcyNqm3kIvlhyNnafuPNlwkOcUO9kouLkEyZK95nZeLSfTluy\ngAGFvAsgXw+fOarW5y70i+NdkAfR8+H4up6Qb65erO3igzNtyA4rTpDtP874B2O6\nlBXbfr7b6f3XCuABjY07nCpxLB53lHMnlt29oK0GAVpYK/xeNsMCvrZGtfZqnnTj\nL8t2MKhKY/3x9G1X7Egv67b3GVVmGoh94FkGhkFr6RZKPyB/xvF5B+m/kIbIxvpI\ni0hdJWJzB4HdFrzkzEtS7t/WyhkmmRIv7Ku/s59pYZC3T1h+ICF5WKei6UBUowT8\nWBOaiJdrL0CGkIlaL/eN7QplPveJA+FuAcFfFavrlOS5kHllSs1QpCX7GyoTq3Zu\n/EgdzVbtlmrwJYqrsPhuuwM14NFq2sgHgwV+tJ3Tk7km7cyWU2oULAgIxOhkl8IE\n/Jx7XTpKBjm4KA4A/ALzGX0GFb0iwbwLduWTB7Z5UpKwr6KnxLvvQC8djuBz8Efj\nATXRySwJH8M6ZK/3g5E8t0HZGFgQSsp9I+G+6f5ybNgrlmD28TKmoItEHBJ1FrBp\n