content.com/u/340520?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis","id":340520,"login":"ferdinandsalis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDUyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/bdd62a3fd3b434fd23edb1faa63b5f24c3faec7e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:34:11Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:34:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rework the FAQ with Agnes: 5 questions become 14 (#129)\n\nNine new questions alongside the five existing ones, written and signed off by\nAgnes, plus a design pass on the section on the landing page.\n\nEvery answer says the one thing you need and links to the page that owns the\ndetail rather than repeating it, so figures, dates and free places stay in one\nplace and the FAQ cannot go stale behind them. A test enforces this: an answer\nsharing a 12-word run with another route file fails CI.\n\nOn the landing page the chips become an accordion that answers in place, ending\nin two doors: whoever is still missing an answer goes to /kontakt, whoever would\nrather come and look goes to the next Termin. Orange now marks the open question\nand nothing else.\n\nAlso: FAQPage structured data on /haeufige-fragen, a title, description and\nfooter link for that page, Plausible events on opening a question, and\n/ueber-uns corrected to ca. 25 Jugendliche per Jahrgang.","tree":{"sha":"e6cea9ee437c71ff2208994ede6b525e71d846e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/e6cea9ee437c71ff2208994ede6b525e71d846e4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/bdd62a3fd3b434fd23edb1faa63b5f24c3faec7e","verification":{"payload":"tree e6cea9ee437c71ff2208994ede6b525e71d846e4\nparent 1fafe4a0ae02c325e75410e3a17ccb060c75948c\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1789493651 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789493651 +0200\n\nRework the FAQ with Agnes: 5 questions become 14 (#129)\n\nNine new questions alongside the five existing ones, written and signed off by\nAgnes, plus a design pass on the section on the landing page.\n\nEvery answer says the one thing you need and links to the page that owns the\ndetail rather than repeating it, so figures, dates and free places stay in one\nplace and the FAQ cannot go stale behind them. A test enforces this: an answer\nsharing a 12-word run with another route file fails CI.\n\nOn the landing page the chips become an accordion that answers in place, ending\nin two doors: whoever is still missing an answer goes to /kontakt, whoever would\nrather come and look goes to the next Termin. Orange now marks the open question\nand nothing else.\n\nAlso: FAQPage structured data on /haeufige-fragen, a title, description and\nfooter link for that page, Plausible events on opening a question, and\n/ueber-uns corrected to ca. 25 Jugendliche per Jahrgang.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqYGTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIlkQADuV8ilA1q4zd89APihs2Do9\nLf8njGfPQjBbYMNCOkmGHaPlU6e7bjEXrSBxa3UFrJyOnqYRAl87Rtn0mptxsRYL\n3cUf7dobzmMaGNzzwE9W