"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/e6c9245042155c620a037acd7a6aa30d430023dd","node_id":"C_kwDOKP_7ZtoAKGU2YzkyNDUwNDIxNTVjNjIwYTAzN2FjZDdhNmFhMzBkNDMwMDIzZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis/walz/commit/e286973fa912d8ac2bae98ee822415959abe453e","sha":"e286973fa912d8ac2bae98ee822415959abe453e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/e286973fa912d8ac2bae98ee822415959abe453e"}],"sha":"e6c9245042155c620a037acd7a6aa30d430023dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/e6c9245042155c620a037acd7a6aa30d430023dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/340520?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ferdinandsalis","id":340520,"login":"ferdinandsalis","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MDUyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ferdinandsalis","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/commits/e286973fa912d8ac2bae98ee822415959abe453e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:41:03Z","email":"mail@ferdinandsalis.com","name":"Ferdinand Salis"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:41:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rework the FAQ: answer inline, and make the page findable (#128)\n\n* Answer the top FAQs on the landing page, from one FAQ source\n\nThe questions were hardcoded twice — as chip links on the landing page and\nas full answers on /haeufige-fragen — and had already drifted (two of the\nfive chips linked to /haeufige-fragen#…, three to /haeufige-fragen/#…).\n\n- Move the questions, teasers and answers into app/routes/__faqs.tsx, which\n  both pages now render from. __ prefixed files are not routes.\n- Replace the landing page chips with an accordion (the ui/accordion\n  component, until now unused) that answers each question in two or three\n  sentences and links on to the full answer, with the first one open. The\n  section is extracted as FaqSection so it can be rendered in a test.\n- Add schema.org FAQPage structured data to /haeufige-fragen, built from the\n  same data, so the markup cannot drift from the visible answers.\n\nThe prose and the links within it are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YD7gwmkfvVpZhz3mEpX3no\n\n* Give the FAQ a way onward, a title and a footer link\n\nFollow-ups to the FAQ rework that are independent of which questions the FAQ\nactually asks:\n\n- Order the existing questions by intent: kennenlernen and kosten lead, the\n  identity and philosophy answers follow. The order drives the landing page,\n  /haeufige-fragen and the structured data alike.\n- Close the landing section with \"Frage nicht dabei?\" → /kontakt, naming the\n  next Kennenlernen-Termin. It reuses closestOrientation, which the loader\n  already fetches and today discards whenever a shoutout is set. Worth noting\n  /kontakt was until now linked from nowhere in the header or footer.\n- Give /haeufige-fragen a title and description — it had neither and inherited\n  the root''s bare \"Walz\" — and link it from the footer. The landing page was\n  its only entrance.\n- Track which questions get opened in Plausible. The tag is deferred, so a\n  queue stub in root.tsx takes calls made before it loads. The \"FAQ Open\" and\n  \"FAQ Read More\" goals still need creating in the Plausible dashboard.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YD7gwmkfvVpZhz3mEpX3no\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc5af55da120197c573bf58883426cafb305b8fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/trees/fc5af55da120197c573bf58883426cafb305b8fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ferdinandsalis/walz/git/commits/e286973fa912d8ac2bae98ee822415959abe453e","verification":{"payload":"tree fc5af55da120197c573bf58883426cafb305b8fc\nparent 12ab85ef25ffccef7d27b85625cc8c2ece3c3998\nauthor Ferdinand Salis <mail@ferdinandsalis.com> 1788464463 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788464463 +0200\n\nRework the FAQ: answer inline, and make the page findable (#128)\n\n* Answer the top FAQs on the landing page, from one FAQ source\n\nThe questions were hardcoded twice — as chip links on the landing page and\nas full answers on /haeufige-fragen — and had already drifted (two of the\nfive chips linked to /haeufige-fragen#…, three to /haeufige-fragen/#…).\n\n- Move the questions, teasers and answers into app/routes/__faqs.tsx, which\n  both pages now render from. __ prefixed files are not routes.\n- Replace the landing page chips with an accordion (the ui/accordion\n  component, until now unused) that answers each question in two or three\n  sentences and links on to the full answer, with the first one open. The\n  section is extracted as FaqSection so it can be rendered in a test.\n- Add schema.org FAQPage structured data to /haeufige-fragen, built from the\n  same data, so the markup cannot drift from the visible answers.\n\nThe prose and the links within it are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YD7gwmkfvVpZhz3mEpX3no\n\n* Give the FAQ a way onward, a title and a footer link\n\nFollow-ups to the FAQ rework that are independent of which questions the FAQ\nactually asks:\n\n- Order the existing questions by intent: kennenlernen and kosten lead, the\n  identity and philosophy answers follow. The order drives the landing page,\n  /haeufige-fragen and the structured data alike.\n- Close the landing section with \"Frage nicht dabei?\" → /kontakt, naming the\n  next Kennenlernen-Termin. It reuses closestOrientation, which the loader\n  already fetches and today discards whenever a shoutout is set. Worth noting\n  /kontakt was until now linked from nowhere in the header or footer.\n- Give /haeufige-fragen a title and description — it had neither and inherited\n  the root''s bare \"Walz\" — and link it from the footer. The landing page was\n  its only entrance.\n- Track which questions get opened in Plausible. The tag is deferred, so a\n  queue stub in root.tsx takes calls made before it loads. The \"FAQ Open\" and\n  \"FAQ Read More\" goals still need creating in the Plausible dashboard.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YD7gwmkfvVpZhz3mEpX3no\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmc1PCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiGQQAG9V5t7/47OWW6rT1bWzRdSc\nGf7NydSdhm+D5bX4xD6CrZkA83f0t5K9frakM/TQbW7OmKgmxo8K6u5SoMV74XvH\nYASutUNA3xFdG0qLSPczSkI6tBYcDDJEKQZQMhngrslB/p7dHD3hrsy+EChCaUX4\nyy5M8lBfbbQLd2FSb6K3a6k6Uc8XTydchG6OjicHIXaC+NQ8TT6+JIeuNn6zbvqG\nICDgZpiVTLNfR9PbV+jiyZ17NPIi4jOGtQ89Hb2H/x9wK3DBFOjerPX6e8K9+Lse\n6chtEtlDdtDyqiWVTiM9QOdbG3o1Z9LSyaZHyxQf80VEe4RRgA3AaJyS0MrkDgI/\nSfisMLYYA5byoMvvzEWVX0tBUNVpiCYww7AbH7XnSlp22XTvWVbDk1jvOq7tMlHj\np3HvMJxzw4RsIc1OEbu0bkkcxm+fpZm7MP6SewRL5/RFn97qo5L+GfuTACwRNpm8\naA7OSdMCNPz6dmSM/krsOrIwZWQwbpp+S5GvjiWSs/